g. Non-discrimination;
h. Confidentiality of victims;
i. Anti-violence;
j. Empowerment of victims;
k. Holistic.

CHAPTER VII

SERVICES FOR VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

Article 13

1. The forms of services provided to women and children victims of acts of violence, are as follows:a. Complaint services;
b. Health services;
c. Legal servicesd. Repatriation;
e. Recovery, social reintegration, and medicolegal;
f. Identification services;
g. Psychological services; andh. Shelter.
2. The forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), are carried out according to minimum service standards established by the Government and carried out by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:a. Social;
b. Economicc. Health;
d. Women empowerment and child protection; ande. Mental and spiritual.
3. In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government cooperates with Government Agencies, other Regional Governments, and the community.
4. Further provisions regarding the procedures for handling services for women and children from acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2) and paragraph (3), are regulated by Regent Regulation.

CHAPTER VI

ROLE OF GOVERNMENT, PRIVATE SECTOR AND COMMUNITY INSTITUTIONS

Article 11

1. To prevent acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government conducts empowerment and awareness to families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling and realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.
2. In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government makes efforts as follows:  a. Increasing the number and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. Providing accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services;
c. Providing employment for women;
d. Building community participation and concern for the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. Building and providing an information system that is easily accessible;
f. Building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children;
g. Optimizing the integrated service center for women empowerment and child protection (P2TP2A) or other designation as a post for the protection of women and children from acts of violence; andh. Opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children based on communities.

CHAPTER V

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 7

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection and Empowerment to women and children are the joint responsibility of:
a. Government/Regional Government and Government Institutions;
b. Private Sector and Community Institutions;
c. Society;
d. Family and or Parents.

Article 12

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 11, is carried out by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:a. Social;
b. Health;
c. Education;
d. Manpower;
e. Women empowerment and child protection;
f. Mental and spiritual; andg. tranquility and public order.
2. Prevention of acts of violence by SKPD as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out in an integrated and continuous manner based on the Regional Action Plan.

REGENT OF CIREBON,

Considering:
a. that children are a trust and gift from Almighty God in whom inherent dignity and worth as complete human beings, and are the next generation of the nation's ideals and struggles, therefore they need to receive protection and the widest possible opportunity for survival, growth and development in a proper manner;
b. that in connection with the large number of women and children who need protection from various forms of violence, mistreatment, exploitation, and neglect, it is deemed necessary to have strategic efforts from the Regional Government and other parties who are obliged to provide protection to the said women and children;
c. that discrimination and violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and crimes against humanity, therefore in order to fulfill the constitutional rights of women and children as referred to in letter b, the Regional Government may carry out coordinated functions in an integrated manner towards the implementation of its duties, authorities, and responsibilities;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection, Empowerment of Women and Children.

